&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Mozilla?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Mozilla Corporation is the non-profit-backed technology company that has shaped the internet for the better over the last 25 years. We make pioneering brands like Firefox, the privacy-minded web browser. Now, with more than 225 million people around the world using our products each month, we’re shaping the next 25 years of technology and helping to reclaim an internet built for people, not companies. Our work focuses on diverse areas including AI, social media, security and more. And we’re doing this while never losing our focus on our core mission – to make the internet better for people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The Mozilla Corporation is wholly owned by the non-profit 501(c) Mozilla Foundation. This means we aren’t beholden to any shareholders — only to our mission. Along with thousands of volunteer contributors and collaborators all over the world, Mozillians design, build and distribute &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;open-source&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; software that enables people to enjoy the internet on their terms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design, build and implement security and hardening features for enterprise users:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Design, implement, test, and ship cutting-edge security features that strengthen Firefox’s security posture.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advance Firefox’s security architecture across multiple operating systems: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Contribute to and drive cutting-edge improvements to Firefox’s core security posture, by building privilege isolation and moving trust boundaries &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;or Strengthen Firefox’s security architecture:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Improve Firefox’s core security mechanisms including cryptographic protocols, WebPKI, and security-sensitive web APIs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to our security initiatives:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Work across teams to investigate security issues, identify root causes, and deliver robust, maintainable fixes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve browser reliability and performance:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Diagnose and resolve issues affecting stability, correctness, performance, and memory usage in a complex, multithreaded environment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
